H6400.definition:
from H6398 (פָּלַח);
a slice
KJV: piece.

H6401.definition:
from H6400 (פֶּלַח); slicing;
Pilcha, an Israelite
KJV: Pilcha.

H6403.definition:
a primitive root;
to slip out, i.e. escape; causatively, to deliver
KJV: calve, carry away safe, deliver, (cause to) escape.

H6404.definition:
from H6403 (פָּלַט); escape;
Pelet, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Pelet. See also H1046 (בֵּית פֶּלֶט).

H6405.definition:
from H6403 (פָּלַט);
escape
KJV: deliverance, escape.

H6406.definition:
from H6403 (פָּלַט); delivered;
Palti, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Palti, Phalti.

H6407.definition:
patronymically from H6406 (פַּלְטִי);
a Paltite or descendant of Palti
KJV: Paltite.

H6408.definition:
for H6407 (פַּלְטִי);
Piltai, an Israelite
KJV: Piltai.

H6409.definition:
from the same as H6404 (פֶּלֶט) and H410 (אֵל); deliverance of God;
Paltiel, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Paltiel, Phaltiel.

H6410.definition:
or פְּלַטְיָהוּ; from H6403 (פָּלַט) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has delivered;
Pelatjah, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Pelatiah.

H6411.definition:
or פְּלָאיָה; from H6381 (פָּלָא) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has distinguished;
Pelajah, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Pelaiah.

H6412.definition:
or פָּלֵיט; or פָּלֵט; from H6403 (פָּלַט);
a refugee
KJV: (that have) escape(-d, -th), fugitive.

H6413.definition:
or פְּלֵטָה; feminine of H6412 (פָּלִיט);
deliverance; concretely, an escaped portion
KJV: deliverance, (that is) escape(-d), remnant.

H6414.definition:
from H6419 (פָּלַל);
a magistrate
KJV: judge.

H6415.definition:
feminine of H6414 (פָּלִיל);
justice
KJV: judgment.

H6417.definition:
feminine of H6416 (פְּלִילִי);
judicature
KJV: judgment.

H6418.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be round;
a circuit (i.e. district); also a spindle (as whirled); hence, a crutch
KJV: (di-) staff, participle

H6419.definition:
a primitive root;
to judge (officially or mentally); by extension, to intercede, pray
KJV: intreat, judge(-ment), (make) pray(-er, -ing), make supplication.

H6420.definition:
from H6419 (פָּלַל); judge;
Palal, an Israelite
KJV: Palal.

H6421.definition:
from H6419 (פָּלַל) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has judged;
Pelaljah, an Israelite
KJV: Pelaliah.

H6422.definition:
probably for H6423 (פְּלֹנִי);
a certain one, i.e. so-and-so
KJV: certain.

H6423.definition:
from H6395 (פָּלָה);
such a one, i.e. a specified person
KJV: such.

H6424.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to roll flat, i.e. prepare (a road); also to revolve, i.e. weigh (mentally)
KJV: make, ponder, weigh.

H6425.definition:
from H6424 (פָּלַס);
a balance
KJV: scales, weight.

H6426.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, perhaps to rend, i.e. (by implication) to quiver
KJV: tremble.

H6427.definition:
from H6426 (פָּלַץ);
affright
KJV: fearfulness, horror, trembling.

H6428.definition:
a primitive root;
to roll (in dust)
KJV: roll (wallow) self.

H6429.definition:
from H6428 (פָּלַשׁ); rolling, i.e. migratory;
Pelesheth, a region of Syria
KJV: Palestina, Palestine, Philistia, Philistines.

H6430.definition:
patrial from H6429 (פְּלֶשֶׁת);
a Pelishtite or inhabitant of Pelesheth
KJV: Philistine.

H6431.definition:
from an unused root meaning to flee; swiftness;
Peleth, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Peleth.

H6432.definition:
from the same form as H6431 (פֶּלֶת);
a courier (collectively) or official messenger
KJV: Pelethites.

H6433.definition:
(Aramaic) probably for H6310 (פֶּה);
the mouth (literally or figuratively)
KJV: mouth.

H6434.definition:
from an unused root meaning to turn;
an angle (of a street or wall)
KJV: corner.

H6435.definition:
from H6437 (פָּנָה);
properly, removal; used only (in the construction) adverb as conjunction, lest
KJV: (lest) (peradventure), that...not.

H6436.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
probably pastry
KJV: Pannag.

H6437.definition:
a primitive root;
to turn; by implication, to face, i.e. appear, look, etc.
KJV: appear, at (even-) tide, behold, cast out, come on, [idiom] corner, dawning, empty, go away, lie, look, mark, pass away, prepare, regard, (have) respect (to), (re-) turn (aside, away, back, face, self), [idiom] right (early).

H6438.definition:
feminine of H6434 (פֵּן);
an angle; by implication, a pinnacle; figuratively, a chieftain
KJV: bulwark, chief, corner, stay, tower.

H6439.definition:
or (more properly,) פְּנִיאֵל; from H6437 (פָּנָה) and H410 (אֵל); face of God;
Penuel or Peniel, a place East of Jordan; also (as Penuel) the name of two Israelites
KJV: Peniel, Penuel.

H6440.definition:
plural (but always as singular) of an unused noun פָּנֶה; from H6437 (פָּנָה));
the face (as the part that turns); used in a great variety of applications (literally and figuratively); also (with prepositional prefix) as a preposition (before, etc.)
KJV: [phrase] accept, a-(be-) fore(-time), against, anger, [idiom] as (long as), at, [phrase] battle, [phrase] because (of), [phrase] beseech, countenance, edge, [phrase] employ, endure, [phrase] enquire, face, favour, fear of, for, forefront(-part), form(-er time, -ward), from, front, heaviness, [idiom] him(-self), [phrase] honourable, [phrase] impudent, [phrase] in, it, look(-eth) (-s), [idiom] me, [phrase] meet, [idiom] more than, mouth, of, off, (of) old (time), [idiom] on, open, [phrase] out of, over against, the partial, person, [phrase] please, presence, propect, was purposed, by reason of, [phrase] regard, right forth, [phrase] serve, [idiom] shewbread, sight, state, straight, [phrase] street, [idiom] thee, [idiom] them(-selves), through ([phrase] -out), till, time(-s) past, (un-) to(-ward), [phrase] upon, upside ([phrase] down), with(-in, [phrase] -stand), [idiom] ye, [idiom] you.

H6441.definition:
from H6440 (פָּנִים) with directive enclitic;
faceward, i.e. indoors
KJV: (with-) in(-ner part, -ward).

H6443.definition:
or פָּנִי; from the same as H6434 (פֵּן);
probably a pearl (as round)
KJV: ruby.

H6444.definition:
probably feminine from H6443 (פָּנִין) contr.;
Peninnah, an Israelitess
KJV: Peninnah.

H6445.definition:
a primitive root;
to enervate
KJV: bring up.

H6446.definition:
from H6461 (פָּסַס); properly, the palm (of the hand) or sole (of the foot) (compare H6447 (פַּס)); by implication (plural)
a long and sleeved tunic (perhaps simply a wide one; from the original sense of the root, i.e. of many breadths)
KJV: (divers) colours.

H6447.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H6461 (פָּסַס);
the palm (of the hand, as being spread out)
KJV: participle

H6448.definition:
a primitive root;
to cut up, i.e. (figuratively) contemplate
KJV: consider.

H6449.definition:
from H6448 (פָּסַג); a cleft;
Pisgah, a Mountain East of Jordan
KJV: Pisgah.

H6450.definition:
from H6446 (פַּס) and the plural of H1818 (דָּם); palm (i.e. dell) of bloodshed;
Pas-Dammim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Pas-dammim. Compare H658 (אֶפֶס דַּמִּים).

H6451.definition:
from H6461 (פָּסַס);
expansion, i.e. abundance
KJV: handful.

H6452.definition:
a primitive root;
to hop, i.e. (figuratively) skip over (or spare); by implication, to hesitate; also (literally) to limp, to dance
KJV: halt, become lame, leap, pass over.

H6453.definition:
from H6452 (פָּסַח);
a pretermission, i.e. exemption; used only techically of the Jewish Passover (the festival or the victim)
KJV: passover (offering).

H6454.definition:
from H6452 (פָּסַח); limping;
Paseach, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Paseah, Phaseah.

H6456.definition:
from H6458 (פָּסַל);
an idol
KJV: carved (graven) image, quarry.

H6457.definition:
from an unused root meaning to divide; divider;
Pasak, an Israelite
KJV: Pasach.

H6458.definition:
a primitive root;
to carve, whether wood or stone
KJV: grave, hew.

H6459.definition:
from H6458 (פָּסַל);
an idol
KJV: carved (graven) image.

H6461.definition:
a primitive root;
probably to disperse, i.e. (intransitive) disappear
KJV: cease.

H6462.definition:
perhaps from H6461 (פָּסַס); dispersion;
Pispah, an Israelite
KJV: Pispah.

H6463.definition:
a primitive root;
to scream
KJV: cry.

H6464.definition:
or פָּעִי; from H6463 (פָּעָה); screaming;
Pau or Pai, a place in Edom
KJV: Pai, Pau.

H6465.definition:
from H6473 (פָּעַר); a gap; also H1187 (בַּעַל פְּעוֹר))
Peor, a mountain East of Jordan; Baal Peor,  (for a deity worshipped there
KJV: Peor. See also H1047 (בֵּית פְּעוֹר).

H6466.definition:
a primitive root;
to do or make (systematically and habitually), especially to practise
KJV: commit, (evil-) do(-er), make(-r), ordain, work(-er).

H6467.definition:
from H6466 (פָּעַל);
an act or work (concretely)
KJV: act, deed, do, getting, maker, work.

H6468.definition:
feminine passive participle of H6466 (פָּעַל);
(abstractly) work
KJV: labour, reward, wages, work.

H6469.definition:
from H6468 (פְּעֻלָּה); laborious;
Peullethai, an Israelite
KJV: Peulthai.

H6470.definition:
a primitive root;
to tap, i.e. beat regularly; hence (generally) to impel or agitate
KJV: move, trouble.

H6471.definition:
or (feminine) פַּעֲמָה; from H6470 (פָּעַם);
a stroke, literally or figuratively (in various applications, as follow)
KJV: anvil, corner, foot(-step), going, (hundred-) fold, [idiom] now, (this) [phrase] once, order, rank, step, [phrase] thrice, (often-), second, this, two) time(-s), twice, wheel.

H6472.definition:
from H6471 (פַּעַם);
a bell (as struck)
KJV: bell.

H6473.definition:
a primitive root;
to yawn, i.e. open wide (literally or figuratively)
KJV: gape, open (wide).

H6474.definition:
from H6473 (פָּעַר); yawning;
Paarai, an Israelite
KJV: Paarai.

H6475.definition:
a primitive root;
to rend, i.e. open (especially the mouth)
KJV: deliver, gape, open, rid, utter.

H6476.definition:
a primitive root;
to break out (in joyful sound)
KJV: break (forth, forth into joy), make a loud noise.

H6478.definition:
a primitive root;
to peel
KJV: pill.

H6479.definition:
from H6478 (פָּצַל);
a peeling
KJV: strake.

H6480.definition:
a primitive root;
to rend (by earthquake)
KJV: break.

H6481.definition:
a primitive root;
to split, i.e. wound
KJV: wound.

H6482.definition:
from H6481 (פָּצַע);
a wound
KJV: wound(-ing).

H6483.definition:
from an unused root meaning to dissever; dispersive;
Pitstsets, a priest
KJV: Apses (including the article).

H6484.definition:
a primitive root;
to peck at, i.e. (figuratively) stun or dull
KJV: press, urge, stubbornness.

H6485.definition:
a primitive root;
to visit (with friendly or hostile intent); by analogy, to oversee, muster, charge, care for, miss, deposit, etc.
KJV: appoint, [idiom] at all, avenge, bestow, (appoint to have the, give a) charge, commit, count, deliver to keep, be empty, enjoin, go see, hurt, do judgment, lack, lay up, look, make, [idiom] by any means, miss, number, officer, (make) overseer, have (the) oversight, punish, reckon, (call to) remember(-brance), set (over), sum, [idiom] surely, visit, want.

H6486.definition:
feminine passive participle of H6485 (פָּקַד);
visitation (in many senses, chiefly official)
KJV: account, (that have the) charge, custody, that which...laid up, numbers, office(-r), ordering, oversight, [phrase] prison, reckoning, visitation.

H6487.definition:
from H6485 (פָּקַד);
a deposit
KJV: that which was delivered (to keep), store.

H6489.definition:
from H6485 (פָּקַד); punishment;
Pekod, a symbolic name for Babylon
KJV: Pekod.

H6490.definition:
or פִּקֻּד; from H6485 (פָּקַד);
properly, appointed, i.e. a mandate (of God; plural only, collectively, for the Law)
KJV: commandment, precept, statute.

H6491.definition:
a primitive root;
to open (the senses, especially the eyes); figuratively, to be observant
KJV: open.

H6492.definition:
from H6491 (פָּקַח); watch;
Pekach, an Israelite king
KJV: Pekah.

H6493.definition:
from H6491 (פָּקַח);
clear-sighted; figuratively, intelligent
KJV: seeing, wise.

H6494.definition:
from H6491 (פָּקַח) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has observed;
Pekachjah, an Israelite king
KJV: Pekahiah.

H6495.definition:
from H6491 (פָּקַח) redoubled;
opening (of a dungeon), i.e. jail-delivery (figuratively, salvation for sin)
KJV: opening of the prison.

H6496.definition:
from H6485 (פָּקַד);
a superintendent (civil, military or religious)
KJV: which had the charge, governor, office, overseer, (that) was set.

H6497.definition:
from an unused root meaning to burst; only used as an architectural term of an ornament similar to H6498 (פַּקֻּעָה),
a semi-globe
KJV: knop.

H6498.definition:
from the same as H6497 (פֶּקַע);
the wild cucumber (from splitting open to shed its seeds)
KJV: gourd.

H6499.definition:
or פָּר; from H6565 (פָּרַר);
a bullock (apparently as breaking forth in wild strength, or perhaps as dividing the hoof)
KJV: ([phrase] young) bull(-ock), calf, ox.
